Desktop Linux enumerates V4L2 codecs as /dev/videoN and the request-API
media controller as /dev/mediaN. The GPU sandbox allowlist is the
ChromeOS names (/dev/video-decN, /dev/video-encN, /dev/media-decN) and
only the first few of each. A udev rule publishes Apple AVD and AVE
under those names. This patch makes the non-ChromeOS lookup use the
same names and the same ten-node scan.

The Linux pixel-format filter stays. A camera that happens to be
symlinked onto one of these names is still rejected: a decoder or
encoder input queue must be coded formats (H264, H264_SLICE, HEVC_SLICE,
VP9_FRAME, and the other entries in is_video_format), and the other
queue must be a raw pixel format. ChromeOS behavior is unchanged,
including the legacy unnumbered /dev/video-dec node.

